# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 usual.cc sqrt, the exact complex branch. An imaginary part b that is exactly 0 but that ratnormal leaves as an expression (im(z^2+1) for z=acosh(10^-6) holds ln((10^-6)^2+(...)^2)/2, whose argument is exactly 1), beside a negative real part a: the form sqrt(2*(a+rho))/2*(1+i*b/(a+rho)) has a+rho = 0 and b = 0, so its evalf was 0 or noise at every Digits: sqrt(acosh(10^-6)^2+1) gave 8.4E-8-4.3E-7*i (right 1.21136202627*i), and asinh(acosh(10^-6)) (ln(x+sqrt(x^2+1))) the ln of x alone, -0.4516+1.5708*i (right 1.02322665303+1.57079632679*i). sqrt(acosh(10^-6)^2) was refused with Overflow. Now, where the evalf of b is within 1e-10 of 0 relative to a < 0 (doubles of the evalf), a b that recursive_normal (Giac's user-level normal, which simplifies inside ln) proves 0 gives sqrt(a).
